  "title": "Kourovka problem 4.40 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let C be a fixed non-trivial group (for instance, C = Z/2Z). As it is shown in\n(Yu. I. Merzlyakov, Algebra and Logic, 9, no. 5 (1970), 326–337), for any two groups\nA and B, all split extensions of B by A can be imbedded in a certain unified way into\nthe direct product A × Aut (B ≀ C). How are they situated in it? Yu. I. Merzlyakov",
